            "text": "// The code in the game disables console.log.\n// Back it up in case we want to log something.\nconsole.log2 = console.log;\n\n// Don't edit this in console or you'll get something very fun.\nvar GameConfig = {\n\t// Reference value of refresh rate.\n\trefreshRate: {\n\t\t// Game will be broken if actual instant FPS is higher than this, but will not if instant FPS is lower than this.\n\t\treferenceFPS: 60,\n\t\t// Appears to affect nothing.\n\t\treferenceTPS: 60,\n\t},\n\t// Adaptive tick scheduling\n\tticking: {\n\t\t// Bounds of adaptive tick rate adjustment\n\t\tminTPS: null,\n\t\tmaxTPS: null,\n\t\t// Alternative scheduling method, not as smooth as the default one.\n\t\tuseEvenTickTimeDistribution: false,\n\t\t// Do a zero-time step if a step cannot be made in the current frame.\n\t\tensureTickEveryFrame: false,\n\t\t// Replicate a bug in the previous revision. Can cause very cursed behavior.\n\t\t// For fun only. Keep false if you want the game to work properly.\n\t\tquantumEdition: false,\n\t\t// 0: Default, do unscheduled ticking for stage and scheduled ticking for physics.\n\t\t// Negative integer: Both scheduled, multiple physics ticks per stage tick,\n\t\t// Positive integer: Both scheduled, multiple stage ticks per physics ticks \n\t\tquantumFactor: 0,\n\t},\n\t// Manual zooming\n\tzooming: {\n\t\t// When the user has zoomed out manually beyond lockScale, only allow automatically returning to lockScale,\n\t\t// so the camera will not zoom further into the game unless done manually.\n\t\t// Makes it possible to always view the level fully when playing on devices with small screens.\n\t\tlockAtMinScale: true,\n\t\t// Used to determine the min scale: How full should be level fill the screen at min scale?\n\t\tminScaleRatio: 0.9,\n\t\t// Used to determine the lock scale: \n\t\tlockScaleRatio: 0.97,\n\t},\n\t// Cheating flags.\n\tcheating: {\n\t\tisInvulnerable: false,\n\t\tisFullUnlock: false,\n\t},\n};\n\n// Main enclosure for everything